      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_fc65a93f",
      "@type": "Scene",
      "instance_name": "cracker_presidents_metaphor",
      "label": "a visual metaphor comparing U.S. presidents to different types of crackers",
      "description": "The scene depicts a row of various crackers arranged in columns, visually representing U.S. presidents. The text overlay 'a short history of u.s. presidents' explicitly frames this arrangement as a metaphor. The spatial arrangement of the crackers in columns suggests a chronological or categorical progression, implying a simplistic or trivialized view of presidential history. The scene uses the visual similarity in shape and texture to create a humorous or satirical comparison, reducing complex political figures to snack foods.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
